wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Birla Mandir, Hyderabad"},{"id":"hyderabad_buddha_statue_of_hyderabad","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Buddha Statue of Hyderabad","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":17.41556,"lng":78.475},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_buddha_statue_of_hyderabad","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":16,"commonsNearby":38,"wikiPageviews":2899,"wikidataSitelinks":11,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["buddhastatueofhyderabad","hyderabad"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Buddha Statue of Hyderabad is a monolith located in Hyderabad, Telangana, India. It is the world's tallest monolith of Gautama Buddha, erected on Gibraltar Rock in the middle of Hussain Sagar lake.17°15′29.64″N 78°40′47.51″E","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Buddha Statue of Hyderabad"},{"id":"hyderabad_falaknuma_palace","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Falaknuma Palace","category":"monument","tags":["history","art","photo"],"location":{"lat":17.33095,"lng":78.4675},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_falaknuma_palace","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":3,"commonsNearby":29,"wikiPageviews":4834,"wikidataSitelinks":17,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["falaknumapalace","hyderabad"],"hours":{"week":[null,{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Closed Mon; Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Falaknuma Palace is a palace and a luxury hotel in Hyderabad, Telangana, India. It originally belonged to the Paigah family, and was later owned by the Nizam of Hyderabad. It is on a hillock and covers a 13-hectare (32-acre) area in Falaknuma, 5 kilometres (3.1 mi) from Charminar.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Falaknuma Palace"},{"id":"hyderabad_bhagyalakshmi_temple","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Bhagyalakshmi Temple","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":17.36139,"lng":78.47444},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_bhagyalakshmi_temple","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":10,"commonsNearby":436,"wikiPageviews":908,"wikidataSitelinks":5,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["bhagyalakshmitemple","hyderabad"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Bhagyalakshmi temple is a shrine dedicated to a Hindu goddess located in Hyderabad, India. This temple is located adjacent to the city's historic monument Charminar. Charminar is under care of Archaeological Survey of India (ASI), while a Hindu trust manages the temple dedicated to the Goddess Bhagyalakshmi.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Bhagyalakshmi Temple"},{"id":"hyderabad_nehru_zoological_park","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Nehru Zoological Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":17.35111,"lng":78.44972},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_nehru_zoological_park","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.hyderabadzoo.in","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":33,"commonsNearby":59,"wikiPageviews":907,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["nehruzoologicalpark","hyderabad"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:30","close":"17:30"},{"open":"08:30","close":"17:30"},{"open":"08:30","close":"17:30"},{"open":"08:30","close":"17:30"},null,{"open":"08:30","close":"17:30"},{"open":"08:30","close":"17:30"}],"note":"Closed Fri"},"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Nehru Zoological Park is a zoo located near Mir Alam Tank in Bahadurpura, Telangana, India. It is one of the most visited destinations in Hyderabad.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Nehru Zoological Park"},{"id":"hyderabad_char_kaman","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Char Kaman","category":"landmark","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":17.36222,"lng":78.47472},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_char_kaman","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":363,"wikiPageviews":402,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["charkaman","hyderabad"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Char Kaman are four historical arches in Hyderabad, India. Originally demarcating an open square, they face the four cardinal directions.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Char Kaman"},{"id":"hyderabad_jagannath_temple_hyderabad","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Jagannath Temple, Hyderabad","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":17.41515,"lng":78.42623},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_jagannath_temple_hyderabad","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://shrijagannathtemplehyderabad.com","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":46,"commonsNearby":12,"wikiPageviews":608,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["jagannathtemplehyderabad","hyderabad"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"The Jagannath Temple in Hyderabad, India, Telangana, is a modern temple built by the Odia community of the city of Hyderabad dedicated to the Hindu God Jagannath. The temple located near Banjara hills Road no.12 (twelve) in Hyderabad is famous for its annual Rathyatra festival attended by thousands of devotees.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Jagannath Temple, Hyderabad"},{"id":"hyderabad_sudha_cars_museum","areaId":"hy