t, also known as Chiraan Fort Palace, and Devdi Fareed Nawaz Jung, or Devdi Nazir Nawaz Jung, was built in 1880 by Sir Viqar-ul-Umra, Amir of the Great Paigah Dynasty of Deccan, who served as Prime Minister of Hyderabad.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Chiraan Fort Palace"},{"id":"hyderabad_golden_threshold","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Golden Threshold","category":"landmark","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":17.38828,"lng":78.47415},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_golden_threshold","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":85,"wikiPageviews":218,"wikidataSitelinks":5,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["goldenthreshold","hyderabad"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Golden Threshold is an off-campus annexe of University of Hyderabad. It is named after the renowned Indian poet and political leader Sarojini Naidu's eponymous first collection of poems. It is located near Nampally Station Road, in the Abids neighbourhood of Hyderabad.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Golden Threshold"},{"id":"hyderabad_state_central_library","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"State Central Library","category":"landmark","tags":["history","photo","art"],"location":{"lat":17.3742,"lng":78.4783},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"hyderabad_state_central_library","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":10,"commonsNearby":9,"wikiPageviews":389,"wikidataSitelinks":9,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["statecentrallibrary","hyderabad"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The State Central Library Hyderabad, known as the State Central Library (SCL) and earlier known as Kutub Khana Asafia, is a public library in Hyderabad, Telangana. The library was first established in 1891 at a location in Abids where the General Post Office is today situated.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"State Central Library, Hyderabad"},{"id":"hyderabad_pathargatti","areaId":"hyderabad","name":"Pathargatti","catego